WEBVTT

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:11.333
Thank you for this.

00:00:12.083 --> 00:00:13.333
Happy anniversary.

00:00:13.416 --> 00:00:14.416
Oh.

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:15.875
It's your anniversary?

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:20.166
[George Givot]
♪
This is the night
♪

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:23.250
♪
It's a beautiful night
♪

00:00:23.333 --> 00:00:29.041
-♪
And we call it bella notte
♪
-[Russ sings along]

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:34.791
[sniffs]

00:00:35.708 --> 00:00:37.625
How are we gonna
find them now?

00:00:37.708 --> 00:00:38.708
[sea lion grunts]

00:00:39.708 --> 00:00:40.708
[growls]

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:44.625
-[coin clinking]
-Thanks, seal.

00:00:44.708 --> 00:00:46.000
-[snarling]
-[Truffler shouts]

00:00:46.541 --> 00:00:48.583
Friend. No, no, no!

00:00:48.666 --> 00:00:49.875
I'm sorry. I'm sorry!

00:00:49.958 --> 00:00:51.458
[Truffler shouts]

00:00:52.208 --> 00:00:53.875
[Nibbles]
Just a little farther.

00:00:53.958 --> 00:00:56.500
Jesús and all the answers
you'll ever need

00:00:56.583 --> 00:00:58.000
are, uh, right here

00:00:58.083 --> 00:01:00.958
at the end of this
very scary, dark hallway.

00:01:01.041 --> 00:01:02.875
Boy, this is so much better

00:01:02.958 --> 00:01:04.916
than sitting on a beach
on Outback Island,

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:07.041
sipping piña koalas.

00:01:07.125 --> 00:01:09.708
Hmm. We are not skipping town

00:01:09.791 --> 00:01:13.000
when there is an innocent
snake out there who needs us.

00:01:13.083 --> 00:01:15.791
He's got help:
his motorcycle buddy.

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:16.958
Ah! [pants]

00:01:17.541 --> 00:01:20.208
You are acting weird.
What is your problem?

00:01:20.291 --> 00:01:22.375
Well, A, you railroaded me.

00:01:22.458 --> 00:01:24.083
And B... [inhales]

00:01:24.166 --> 00:01:25.666
...if you must know,

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:30.041
I have an aversion
to reptiles.

00:01:30.125 --> 00:01:31.958
[chuckling] What?

00:01:32.041 --> 00:01:35.875
Oh, is my discomfort
hilarious to you?

00:01:35.958 --> 00:01:38.666
No, you're... I'm sorry.
You're right, we are partners.

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:40.125
And whenever
I'm uncomfortable,

00:01:40.208 --> 00:01:42.625
you are always very
considerate of my feelings.

00:01:42.708 --> 00:01:43.541
Look out! Snake skin!

00:01:43.625 --> 00:01:44.583
-[Judy laughs]
-[Nick growls]

00:01:44.666 --> 00:01:45.666
-Ow!
-I'm slipping!

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:46.666
I'm slipping! Hold the rail!

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:48.083
-I'm holding the rail.
-Hold it. Hold it.

00:01:48.166 --> 00:01:49.250
-Stop pulling my ears!
-Hold the rail.

00:01:49.333 --> 00:01:50.166
Never pull a bunny's ears!

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:52.041
-Hold the rail.
-Never pull a bunny's ears!

00:01:52.125 --> 00:01:53.625
[creaking]

00:01:54.958 --> 00:01:56.875
I think the real mystery

00:01:57.500 --> 00:01:59.500
is how you two
ever solved anything.

00:01:59.583 --> 00:02:01.125
[laughs]

00:02:01.208 --> 00:02:03.750
Anyhoo, let's see what Jesús
has to say about your journal.

00:02:03.833 --> 00:02:06.333
Oh, and if he offers you food,
accept.

00:02:07.375 --> 00:02:09.208
Declining is a sign
of disrespect,

00:02:09.291 --> 00:02:10.458
to all of them.

00:02:10.541 --> 00:02:12.041
"All of them"?

00:02:12.125 --> 00:02:13.416
[door rumbles]

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:15.583
[♪ banjo music playing]

00:02:16.291 --> 00:02:17.416
[chatter, laughter]

00:02:22.708 --> 00:02:24.208
-[shudders]
-Ha! [laughs]

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:26.583
[groans]

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:29.875
[playing jazz]

00:02:36.041 --> 00:02:37.041
Order up.

00:02:38.541 --> 00:02:40.000
Hey, another drink.

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:41.500
[belches]

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:44.000
[whimpers]

00:02:46.541 --> 00:02:47.875
So warm.

00:02:48.375 --> 00:02:49.333
-Gah!
-[gecko shouts]

00:02:49.416 --> 00:02:50.250
[crunch]

00:02:50.916 --> 00:02:52.291
Whoops.

00:02:52.375 --> 00:02:53.375
No!

00:02:54.625 --> 00:02:56.791
[chuckles] Keep it.

00:02:58.166 --> 00:02:59.166
[shudders]

00:03:00.791 --> 00:03:03.000
[Nibbles] Jesús!

00:03:03.083 --> 00:03:04.666
Allow me to introduce
my friends.

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:06.541
This is Judith and Nicholas.

00:03:06.625 --> 00:03:08.000
They are wanted fugitives

00:03:08.083 --> 00:03:09.416
investigating a snake mystery

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:10.791
and trying
not to get murdered.

00:03:10.875 --> 00:03:12.208
May we sit?

00:03:15.666 --> 00:03:16.666
-[snapping]
-Oh. Okay.

00:03:17.208 --> 00:03:18.833
[all straining]

00:03:20.791 --> 00:03:22.125
[Judy squeals]

00:03:23.583 --> 00:03:25.791
Oh, I'm good,
but these guys look hungry.

00:03:30.083 --> 00:03:31.500
Thank you for meeting with us.

00:03:31.583 --> 00:03:34.833
We believe snakes were framed
for something in this journal,

00:03:34.916 --> 00:03:38.625
-perhaps pertaining to...
-Eat first, talk second.

00:03:39.166 --> 00:03:40.000
Oh.

00:03:41.291 --> 00:03:42.958
[Judy, Nick groan]

00:03:54.791 --> 00:03:56.125
-[whimpers]
-[gags]

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:03.458
[shudders]

00:04:04.916 --> 00:04:05.916
Uh...

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.291
[slurping]

00:04:09.375 --> 00:04:11.166
[gags]

00:04:15.666 --> 00:04:17.666
Hey, guys. They ate it!

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:19.083
-[Jesús laughing]
-[all cheering]

00:04:19.166 --> 00:04:20.791
[Jesús] Look at their faces.
[laughs]

00:04:20.875 --> 00:04:22.333
I don't eat grubs.

00:04:22.416 --> 00:04:24.416
Hermano
, get me a scone!

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:26.000
[Jesús laughs]

00:04:26.083 --> 00:04:27.375
Okay, okay.

00:04:28.458 --> 00:04:29.541
Hmm.

00:04:30.333 --> 00:04:31.791
Metal cover.

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:34.500
And what does that mean?

00:04:34.583 --> 00:04:35.583
It means

00:04:36.916 --> 00:04:37.958
it's fancy.

00:04:39.083 --> 00:04:42.041
It also means
the secret you're looking for

00:04:42.125 --> 00:04:44.083
is probably
right on the cover.

00:04:44.666 --> 00:04:47.583
Somehow vipers can see things
in the metal,

00:04:47.666 --> 00:04:49.583
even under the paint.

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:52.791
This is Ebenezer Lynxley's
original journal

00:04:52.875 --> 00:04:54.041
for the weather walls.

00:04:54.125 --> 00:04:57.833
Why would he hide a secret
for a snake?

00:04:57.916 --> 00:04:59.083
I don't know.

00:04:59.166 --> 00:05:03.166
But it must have been big,
'cause a tortoise died for it.

00:05:03.666 --> 00:05:06.958
I am guessing
that it was a slow death.

00:05:07.791 --> 00:05:09.250
[sighs]

00:05:09.333 --> 00:05:10.333
[Nibbles groans]

00:05:10.416 --> 00:05:14.041
The fanging didn't just change
how folks saw snakes.

00:05:14.791 --> 00:05:17.666
No mammals trusted
any reptile after that.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:18.750
REPTILES:
FRIEND OR FOE?

00:05:18.833 --> 00:05:19.833
WHO ARE THEY
AND CAN WE TRUST THEM

00:05:19.916 --> 00:05:22.083
[Jesús]
That's why we all left.

00:05:22.166 --> 00:05:23.583
And that's when the Lynxleys

00:05:23.666 --> 00:05:26.416
expanded Tundratown
the first time.

00:05:27.875 --> 00:05:29.958
And it's happening again.

00:05:31.166 --> 00:05:33.333
The expansion is going here.

00:05:33.416 --> 00:05:36.916
[inhales] Marsh Market
will be buried in snow.

00:05:38.041 --> 00:05:39.666
We'll all get pushed out.

00:05:40.625 --> 00:05:42.833
Those lynxes
will get more land,

00:05:43.541 --> 00:05:46.208
and there's no way
to stop 'em.

00:05:52.041 --> 00:05:55.458
What if the secret
hidden in here could?

00:05:56.458 --> 00:05:57.916
Then I would say

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:02.833
holding it puts the two of you
in grave danger.

00:06:02.916 --> 00:06:04.083
-[rumbling]
-[both gasp]

00:06:05.166 --> 00:06:06.500
-[rumbling grows louder]
-Ooh.

00:06:09.916 --> 00:06:11.583
-[all yelp]
-They tracked you?

00:06:11.666 --> 00:06:13.250
Hmm-hmm-hmm.

00:06:14.083 --> 00:06:15.083
Whoops.

00:06:15.166 --> 00:06:17.000
-[grunting]
-[all screaming]

00:06:17.083 --> 00:06:19.166
-It's the ZPD!
-[Lizard yelps]

00:06:19.250 --> 00:06:21.791
[slowly] Run!

00:06:21.875 --> 00:06:23.208
Leave the tails!

00:06:23.291 --> 00:06:24.791
Follow me. Come on!

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:29.583
Wait. Why are you helping us?

00:06:29.666 --> 00:06:31.708
You two saved the city once.

00:06:31.791 --> 00:06:33.958
I reckon you can
save it again.

00:06:34.041 --> 00:06:35.833
And when you do,

00:06:35.916 --> 00:06:39.416
maybe everyone will see
we ain't that different.

00:06:40.625 --> 00:06:42.416
[jabbering]

00:06:43.958 --> 00:06:44.875
Huh.

00:06:45.541 --> 00:06:47.416
-Freeze!
-Yeah, freeze!

00:06:48.458 --> 00:06:49.458
I'm really sorry. But this is

00:06:49.541 --> 00:06:51.250
my family's only chance
to come home.

00:06:51.333 --> 00:06:52.500
Wait. We wanna help.

00:06:52.583 --> 00:06:53.916
Wait. Wait.

00:06:55.208 --> 00:06:56.875
Come back!

00:06:56.958 --> 00:06:58.833
There's no path.
Take the docks!

00:06:58.916 --> 00:07:00.000
Wha-- Carrots!

00:07:00.083 --> 00:07:01.875
Wait! We believe you!

00:07:01.958 --> 00:07:03.333
Nick! Come on! Come on!

00:07:03.416 --> 00:07:04.250
[sighs]

00:07:04.333 --> 00:07:05.375
-[thud]
-[Nick yelps]

00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:11.458
[Nick blabbering]

00:07:11.541 --> 00:07:12.583
-[thud]
-Ow!

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:16.000
Grab it!

00:07:21.291 --> 00:07:22.291
Hey!

00:07:23.083 --> 00:07:25.500
I got eyes on them.
They're heading for the tubes!

00:07:25.583 --> 00:07:26.750
In pursuit.

00:07:30.916 --> 00:07:32.875
[Nick grunting]

00:07:35.750 --> 00:07:36.958
[shouting]

00:07:41.625 --> 00:07:42.750
[bells ring]

00:07:43.708 --> 00:07:44.541
Hey, bubba.

00:07:44.625 --> 00:07:45.583
-Hey, bub.
-Hey, bub.

00:07:45.666 --> 00:07:46.500
-Hey, bub.
-Hey, bub.

00:07:47.083 --> 00:07:47.916
Go!

00:07:48.875 --> 00:07:49.750
-Hey, bub.
-Hey, bub.

00:07:49.833 --> 00:07:50.666
-Bub-bye.
-Hey, Bub.

00:07:50.750 --> 00:07:51.583
-Bub-bye.
-Bub-bye.

00:07:51.666 --> 00:07:52.875
Bub-bye. Bye.

00:07:52.958 --> 00:07:54.250
-Hey, bub.
-Bub-bye.

00:07:56.833 --> 00:07:58.500
-[Nick shouts]
-[Nibbles whoops]

00:08:01.583 --> 00:08:04.333
Pro tip! If he goes
for the red line,

00:08:04.416 --> 00:08:06.250
do not follow!

00:08:06.333 --> 00:08:08.708
You will run out of air!

00:08:08.791 --> 00:08:10.833
Good luck! I love you!

00:08:11.625 --> 00:08:13.333
[onlookers gasping]

00:08:15.333 --> 00:08:16.333
Sorry.

00:08:16.958 --> 00:08:17.791
[Gary gulps]

00:08:17.875 --> 00:08:19.458
Cannonball!

00:08:22.333 --> 00:08:23.666
That's a red line. Red line!

00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:26.166
You're going to run out
of air! Coconut! Coconut!

00:08:28.708 --> 00:08:30.291
[muffled screams]

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:48.833
[Duke Weaselton]
Anything you need, I got 'em.

00:08:48.916 --> 00:08:50.708
Sequels, prequels, requels.

00:08:50.791 --> 00:08:52.625
Who says the industry's
going down the tubes?

00:08:52.708 --> 00:08:54.208
[Nick yelling]

00:09:01.166 --> 00:09:02.458
[muffled dialogue]

